User: Points $K$, $L$, $M$, and $N$ lie in the plane of the square $ABCD$ so that $AKB$, $BLC$, $CMD$, and $DNA$ are equilateral triangles. If $ABCD$ has an area of 16, find the area of $KLMN$. Express your answer in simplest radical form.

[asy]
pair K,L,M,I,A,B,C,D;
D=(0,0);
C=(10,0);
B=(10,10);
A=(0,10);
I=(-8.7,5);
L=(18.7,5);
M=(5,-8.7);
K=(5,18.7);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle,linewidth(0.7));
draw(A--D--I--cycle,linewidth(0.7));
